<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis 1996 group net profit down.</title>
<headline>Novartis 1996 group net profit down.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996.</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			2,304	   vs   4,216</p>
<p>Group profit before</p>
<p>   extraordinary items	4,175	   vs   4,096</p>
<p> Dividend (Sfr)		 20.00	   vs   16.80</p>
<p> Turnover			 36,233	  vs  35,943</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of pharmaceuticals and life sciences group, formed through the merger of Ciba-Geigy and Sandoz AG, is Novartis AG.</p>
<p>OPERATING INCOME BY SECTOR:</p>
<p>    Healthcare		  3,900	     vs 3,653</p>
<p>    Agribusiness		1,352	     vs 1,289</p>
<p>    Nutrition		   375		 vs 445</p>
<p>    TOTAL LIFE SCIENCES     5,627	     vs 5,387</p>
<p>Industry (Ciba Specialty</p>
<p>Chemicals MBT, Mettler</p>
<p>Toledo and other divested</p>
<p>    activities)		 960		 vs 1,020</p>
<p>    Corporate,other expense 806		 vs 693</p>
<p> TOTAL OPERATING INCOME     5,781	     vs 5,714</p>
<p> Financial expense, net     245		 vs 288</p>
<p>Exceptional income and</p>
<p> expense			  2,939 (loss)    vs 150 (profit)</p>
<p>Income before taxes and</p>
<p> minority interests	   2,597	     vs 5,576</p>
<p> Taxes			    291		 vs 1,348</p>
<p> Minority interests	   2 (loss)	  vs 12 (loss)</p>
<p> Gross profit		   21,279	    vs 20,725</p>
<p>Marketing, distribution</p>
<p> expense			  8,477	     vs 7,905</p>
<p> R&amp;D spending		   3,656	     vs 3,527</p>
<p>Administration, general</p>
<p> overhead costs		 3,365	     vs 3,579</p>
<p>NOTE: Group turnover data include sales of Ciba Specialty Chemicals, which was spun off earlier this month, and sales from operations since divested.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
